5: #pragma once
6: 
7: /** Grid attribute binding (plan P2): what a kernel's declared attr layers map
8:  * to on the grids domain, and the dense mirror the kernel actually writes.
9:  *
10:  * The routing rule is metadata-only — it reads a BrushAttrManifestEntry, never
11:  * a tool name — so widening it widens the grids roster with no host or
12:  * executor conditional to edit. Four answers:
13:  *
14:  *  - DefaultColumn: a read-only handle whose zero value is a documented,
15:  *    correct default on this domain (BSMOOTH's vclass 0 = plain Laplacian).
16:  *    Binds an executor-owned all-zero column; no storage.
17:  *  - SessionChannel: a kernel-written vertex or face layer, backed by an
18:  *    Authored GridsStore channel plus the dense mirror below. A Host- or
19:  *    Temp-class layer: declareHostAttr is what says the host can store
20:  *    grid-element data for it, and a Derived layer is a cache of the cage
21:  *    that a brush must reach through the cage instead (grid_attrs.h).
22:  *  - LayerScratch: a written SCULPT_LAYER handle under a live edit target —
23:  *    executor-owned per-dab scratch the stage fold turns into co motion,
24:  *    which the stroke-end writeback attributes into the target layer's own
25:  *    channel (Multires::writebackChannel). No storage of its own.
26:  *  - Unbindable: the brush falls back to the materialized-mesh path.
27:  *
28:  * The mirror exists because kernels index a dense mesh::AttrData by element id
29:  * while the store is per-grid with duplicated boundary samples. On the vertex
30:  * domain gather is canonical (one sample per vert, via
31:  * GridLevelDomain::vertGrid) and scatter writes every occurrence, so duplicates
32:  * stay in agreement — the same round-trip GridLevelDomain already uses for
33:  * mask. The face domain has no duplication at all: a grid cell belongs to
34:  * exactly one grid, so both directions are the same flat cell walk. Every copy
35:  * is a memcpy, never float math, which is what keeps a typed (INT) channel
36:  * legal in a float-backed store.
37:  *
38:  * The store is untouched until the stroke-end fold, so undo capture of a
39:  * written channel is a stroke-end captureGrids() immediately before scatter —
40:  * exactly what positions and mask already do. */
41: 
