22: // Falloff curve shapes selectable per brush. The three analytic kinds
23: // inline a closed form; `Curve` reads `Brush::falloff_curve` as a
24: // 256-entry LUT with linear interpolation. `t` is the normalized 0..1
25: // centerwise input â€” 1 at the brush center, 0 at the radius. Smoothstep
26: // is the historical default and keeps regression dumps bit-identical
27: // when no `set_falloff` runs.
28: enum class FalloffKind : unsigned char {
29:   Smoothstep = 0,
30:   Linear = 1,
31:   Gaussian = 2,
32:   Curve = 3,
33: };
34: 
35: // Spatial metric mapping a vertex offset from the brush center to the
36: // normalized 0..1 distance fed into the falloff curve. This is the DSL
37: // plan's `Falloff` tagged-union discriminant, orthogonal to the curve
38: // shape (`FalloffKind`):
39: //   Spherical â€” euclidean radius (historical default, bit-identical).
40: //   Cube      â€” max(|dx|,|dy|,|dz|), the legacy SQUARE-brush metric.
41: //   Linear    â€” distance projected onto `falloff_dir` (stroke-line falloff).
42: //   Box       â€” oriented cuboid: max-norm in an orthonormal frame built from
43: //               `falloff_dir` (primary axis = stroke direction), with
44: //               independent per-axis half-extents in `falloff_extent`.
45: enum class FalloffShape : unsigned char {
46:   Spherical = 0,
47:   Cube = 1,
48:   Linear = 2,
49:   Box = 3,
50: };
