67: // Mapping from a world-space sample point to brush-texture UV. Orthogonal
68: // to the texture data itself; the discriminant rides in BrushUniforms so
69: // the WGSL `brush_sample_tex` mirrors the same branches.
70: //   Global     â€” uv = co.xy (world plane; stroke-independent, the test mode).
71: //   ViewPlane  â€” perspective-project co through renderMatrix (world -> clip),
72: //                NDC remapped to [0,1] across the viewport (screen-pinned).
73: //   ViewRepeat â€” ViewPlane scaled by `tex_repeat` (tiled across the view).
74: //   StrokeCurved â€” uv = (arc length along the stroke, lateral offset from it);
75: //                  reads the StrokePath ring buffer of recent dab centers.
76: //   Projected  â€” project (co - surfacePos) onto the brush-center tangent plane;
77: //                uv = its coordinates in a deterministic orthonormal basis built
78: //                from surfaceNo, normalized so the tile spans the brush circle
79: //                (centered on the dab, 0..1 across the diameter). The one mode
80: //                that actually consumes the surface normal arg threaded through
81: //                sampleBrushTex.
82: enum class TexCoordSpace : unsigned char {
83:   Global = 0,
84:   ViewPlane = 1,
85:   ViewRepeat = 2,
86:   StrokeCurved = 3,
87:   Projected = 4,
88: };
89: } // namespace sculptcore::brush
