5: """
6: The interactive stroke: a modal operator plus the reusable dab core the
7: operator and headless tests both drive.
8: 
9: Dabs are spaced along the 2D mouse path (interval = pixel radius x spacing /
10: 50 — vanilla's percentage-of-diameter semantics, residual carried across
11: segments) and each spaced point is projected onto the surface, so stroke
12: density is independent of both the mouse event rate and the surface deforming
13: under the stroke. The spacing walk is the Python StrokeSpacer below; behind
14: the ``sculptcore_cpp_dab_loop`` scene toggle the emitted points of a plain
15: spaced stroke are then resolved and applied engine-side, batched per pointer
16: event (``_apply_batch``), instead of looped per dab through Python.
17: The viewport updates through the external draw provider; the Mesh ID is
18: written back lazily by the mode's flush callback (memfile encode / save /
19: render), keeping dabs and stroke release free of the full Mesh write. The
20: throttled Mesh flush remains only as the no-provider fallback. The dab core
21: is engine-only (no ``bpy`` state), so ``enter -> N synthetic dabs -> exit``
22: is scriptable end-to-end.
23: """
24: 
25: import bpy
26: 
27: from . import (brush_policy, convert, cursor, engine, mapping, stroke_math, stroke_input,
28:                symmetry, texture, undo)
29: 
30: # Frames presented in any 3D viewport, counted by a draw handler that lives
31: # only while a stroke runs (see _draw_counter_push/_pop). The mid-stroke
32: # refresh cadence gates on it: a refresh whose predecessor no frame has
33: # consumed yet is pure waste — the provider re-fills the same dirty nodes and
34: # only the fill current at draw time is ever uploaded. Wall-clock (30 Hz)
35: # alone over-refreshes exactly when it hurts: event floods and frame-bound
36: # heavy scenes.
37: _frames_presented = 0
38: _draw_counter_handle = None
39: _draw_counter_strokes = 0
40: 
41: # Pointer motion the stroke acts on. INBETWEEN_MOUSEMOVE is a backlog sample
42: # that the window manager demoted rather than discarded, so it carries a real
43: # position, pressure and tilt (see the modal handler).
44: _MOVE_EVENT_TYPES = {'MOUSEMOVE', 'INBETWEEN_MOUSEMOVE'}
45: 
